WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.779
Let's talk now about the Rand Paul story I
mentioned earlier.

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:31.130
Kentucky Republican Senator Rand Paul yesterday
went on Fox News and he chose feelings over

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.130
facts.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.630
I thought they were the facts over feelings,
people.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.400
Rand Paul had a very embarrassing day in total
yesterday.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:42.989
There had they had a Senate hearing where
Dr. Foushee, Dr. Redfield and others testified.

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:49.060
And Rand Paul sort of scolded Anthony Foushee,
telling him, you know, you're not the end-all.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.470
You just want opinion.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:53.370
And we got to look at what other countries
are doing as well, including Sweden, which

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.530
we'll talk about.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.630
But then Rand Paul went on Fox News in the
evening to talk about the new so-called obamma

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.390
Gate scandal.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:06.750
This is a totally fake trumped up scandal
to distract from Donald Trump's incredible

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.899
failure on Corona virus.

00:01:08.899 --> 00:01:14.170
And Rand Paul asserts to Martha MacCallum
that Barack Obama gave direct oversight and

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:18.990
guidance on unmasking Donald Trump's former
national security adviser, Michael Flynn.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:22.890
The Fox News host, Martha MacCallum, asks
the right question, which is, do you have

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.350
evidence of that?

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.640
And Rand Paul says, I'm not I'm not kidding.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.229
You're going to see here I have a strong feeling.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:32.030
He has a feeling, but no facts.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:33.119
Take a look at it.

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:34.200
Trump campaign.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:40.810
I really strongly believe that President Obama
gave specific and direct oversight and direct

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:41.810
permission for this.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:42.810
Think about it.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.240
We have never allowed a secret court to be
used against a presidential campaign.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.800
Don't you think that was sensitive enough
that it went all the way to the very top?

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.149
So, yeah, the media have treated President
Obama with kid gloves.

00:01:54.149 --> 00:01:59.390
One needs to ask him directly, did you approve
a process of operation CROSSFIRE, hurricane

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.890
and other cancers?

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:01.890
Yes.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:06.009
So, you know, I mean, to put the shoe on the
other foot, a lot of it is, do you have evidence

00:02:06.009 --> 00:02:07.009
of that?

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:10.369
You say you're sure that the president, the
former president was involved in this.

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:12.120
Why are you so sure?

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.310
Well, we'll find out.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:17.670
I'm hoping that a lot of this will be declassified,
but I have a strong feeling that this was

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.610
such a sensitive subject.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:23.870
He's already admitted or admitted through
people that worked for him that the Flynn

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.700
investigation he knew a lot about.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.950
And I strongly believe I think the answer
is yes.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:30.950
But do you have evidence?

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:36.840
Well, no, but I have a feeling this is downright
irresponsible for a sitting U.S. senator to

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:41.829
be saying if Rand Paul had a shred of evidence
for his claims, he would have provided it

00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:42.829
by now.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.900
But he doesn't have any evidence.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.660
So instead he has his feelings.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:51.060
Since when do sitting senators go on television
and accuse former presidents of wrongdoing,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.980
allegedly criminal wrongdoing on the basis
of feelings?

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.620
I guess now is the answer to that.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:03.790
So that was Rand Paul choosing feelings over
facts on Fox News earlier in the day.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.189
Here is Rand Paul going after Dr. Foushee.

00:03:06.189 --> 00:03:10.859
Remember that Rand Paul got Corona virus while
he was waiting for his test results.

00:03:10.859 --> 00:03:13.260
He went to the Senate gym and worked out.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.250
Turns out he was positive during that workout.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.950
Now he's refusing to wear a mask.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:22.310
And here he is scolding Dr. Foushee during
yesterday's Senate hearing, which is I respect

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.459
you, Dr. Foushee.

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:24.700
I don't think you're the end at all.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.599
I don't think you're the one person that gets
to make a decision.

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:29.180
We can listen to your advice.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.269
But there are people on the other side saying
there's not going to be a surge and then we

00:03:32.269 --> 00:03:35.150
can safely open the economy and the factual
to bear this out.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.969
But if we keep kids out of school for another
year, what's going to happen is that the poor

00:03:38.969 --> 00:03:42.410
and underprivileged kids who don't have a
parent that's able to teach them at home are

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.489
not going to learn for a full year.

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:47.250
And I think we ought to look at the Swedish
model and we ought to look at letting our

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:48.250
kids get back to school.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.389
Is a huge mistake if we don't open the schools
in the fall.

00:03:51.389 --> 00:03:52.389
Thank you.

00:03:52.389 --> 00:03:54.390
Now, Rand Paul mentioned Sweden.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.480
Let's talk about Sweden a little bit.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:01.000
Sweden, much like chloroquine, has become
a political football.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:05.730
And for me, just like with chloroquine, I
have no emotional attachment to Sweden did

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.459
the right thing or Sweden didn't do the right
thing.

00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:13.859
What happened in Sweden is that older and
vulnerable folks isolated and stayed at home.

00:04:13.859 --> 00:04:15.400
But young people mostly haven't.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.709
There's been mild social distancing in bars
and restaurants.

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:19.709
Schools stayed open.

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:23.180
Young people, for the most part, lived close
to their normal lives.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:24.180
What do we know so far?

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.970
Well, so far, Sweden's death rate is the ninth
highest in the world.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:34.780
If you eliminate tiny countries like San Marino
and Andorra, Sweden's death rate right now

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:39.210
is the sixth highest in the world out of more
than 180 countries.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:45.790
So what we can say is that so far at this
point in the pandemic, Sweden's plan has led

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:48.280
to a really high death rate.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.810
Now, let's be fair.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.260
Does that mean Sweden's plan failed?

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:56.010
Not necessarily, because it's possible.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:05:02.440
It's possible that because Sweden is doing
this and having more a higher death rate now,

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:09.870
it could get them more immunity and potentially,
potentially Sweden could end up with lower

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.420
deaths during wave two and wave three if.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:18.240
There is one, so I again, I just want the
truth.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.200
If Sweden's plan worked, then great.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.200
We should all know it.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.690
If it didn't work, then we should all know
it.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:25.920
So far, Sweden's death rate is very high.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:31.480
But if they end up with more immunity by the
time wave to hits, which could wave to could

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.470
be worse than wave one, we don't know yet.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.950
Sweden may end up in the long term for the
total pandemic.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.290
They could end up with a lower death rate.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:40.290
We just don't know yet.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:43.130
Now, Dr. Foushee responded, I.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:45.510
He also doesn't think he's the be all end
all.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.030
He's just a public health professional.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.100
Here's how he handled it.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.680
First of all, Senator Paul, thank you for
your comments.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:55.280
I have never made myself out to be the end
all and only voice in this.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:58.320
I'm a scientist, a physician and a public
health official.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.190
I give advice according to the best scientific
evidence.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:06.990
There are a number of other people come into
that and give advice that are more related

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:12.660
to the things that you spoke about, the need
to get the country back open again and economically.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.620
I don't give advice about economic things.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:19.140
I don't get advice about anything other than
public health.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.750
So I wanted to respond to that.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:25.150
The second thing is that you use the word
we should be humble about what we don't know.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:30.000
And I think that falls under the fact that
we don't know everything about this virus

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.530
and we really better be very careful, particularly
when it comes to children.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.640
So I think you get the idea.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:38.360
Anthony Foushee not getting rattled by Rand
Paul, making him the enemy.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:43.470
I know we talked about this, but what kind
of a sick country are we that a doctor who's

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.940
been doing this for decades and has worked
for I think it's six presidents is now the

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:47.940
enemy.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:52.420
Bogus documentaries are being made where Dr.
Foushee is the villain.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:57.670
People are attempting to concoct false sexual
assault allegations against Dr. Foushee.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:03.950
As I told you about earlier, crowds at protests
are screaming Fire Foushee.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:07.050
Yesterday I did a story about the world is
laughing at us.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:13.710
The treatment of health experts by the Trump
crowd during this pandemic is a big part of

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:15.450
why the world is laughing at us.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.310
Absolutely sick.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:22.610
And notice, of course, that Dr Foushee has
now been gone for weeks.

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:27.490
From any Trump administration press briefing,
Corona Virus Task Force event, he's still

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:28.490
doing interviews.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:31.610
He testified before the Senate, but he has
been disappeared, as we talk to you about

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:31.632
a couple of weeks ago

